  "question": {
    "text": "In figure, a particle is placed at the highest point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> of a smooth sphere of radius <math><mi>r</mi></math>. It is given slight push, and it leaves the sphere at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, at a depth <math><mi>h</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math>vertically below <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math><mi>h</mi></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/48519_que.JPG\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 169px;\" />",
